      "text": "Thus variation in Cameroon Pidgin English can best be described in terms of a gradatum, as shown in Figure 1 (adapted from Schröder 2003a: 120), with varying degrees of approximation to Cameroon English and to French on the vertical axis and varying degrees of influence from the indigenous languages on the horizontal axis.1 Hence, one finds increasing proximity to English or French and thus anglicised or frenchified variants of Cameroon Pidgin English towards the top of the vertical axis and an assimilated Cameroon Pidgin, which usually reflects strong influence of the indigenous languages, towards the bottom."
